On CUDA the slowest are the partial derivatives of order 6 of Box-Cox (46.5 ns) and Yeo-Johnson (99.5 ns), whose divergent branches and evaluations of the exprel and log1prel derivatives account for most of the runtime; all other operations complete within 4 ns. Across all maps, evaluation requires a few tens of nanoseconds on a single CPU thread and a few nanoseconds on the GPU, except for the order 6 partials of Box-Cox and Yeo-Johnson.

## Example

The following example evaluates the inverse map \f$h(u)\f$ of logit and its first derivative \f$h'(u)\f$ inside a `Kokkos::parallel_for` kernel:

\code{.cpp}
#include <laplace/bijector/scalar.hpp>
#include <Kokkos_Core.hpp>

void evaluate_expit(const Kokkos::View<const double*>& u,
                    Kokkos::View<double*>& h,
                    Kokkos::View<double*>& dh,
                    int n) {
  const laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector b{laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector_map::logit};
  Kokkos::parallel_for("evaluate_expit", n, KOKKOS_LAMBDA(const int i) {
    h(i)  = b.inverse(u(i));
    dh(i) = b.inverse_d1(u(i));
  });
}
\endcode

## Module functions

Functions in this module are member functions of \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector "scalar_bijector".

### Types

- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector_map "scalar_bijector_map" — Enumeration of scalar bijector maps with and without parameters.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector "scalar_bijector" — Scalar bijector configuration structure.
- \ref laplace::bijector::bijector_partials "bijector_partials" — Fixed-size container for partial derivatives in argument and parameters of order up to 6.
- \ref laplace::bijector::bijector_kinks "bijector_kinks" — Description of non-smooth points of a scalar bijector.

### Construction of maps with parameters

- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::affine "affine()" — Constructs an affine bijector with location and scale.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::power "power()" — Constructs a power bijector with exponent.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::softplus "softplus()" — Constructs a softplus bijector with sharpness.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::bounded "bounded()" — Constructs a bounded bijector with lower and upper bounds.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::lower_bounded "lower_bounded()" — Constructs a lower-bounded bijector with lower bound.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::upper_bounded "upper_bounded()" — Constructs an upper-bounded bijector with upper bound.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::box_cox "box_cox()" — Constructs a Box-Cox bijector with exponent.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::yeo_johnson "yeo_johnson()" — Constructs a Yeo-Johnson bijector with exponent.

### Parameter inspection

- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::parameter_1 "parameter_1()" — First parameter of the map, or NaN if none.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::parameter_2 "parameter_2()" — Second parameter of the map, or NaN if none.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::parameter_count "parameter_count()" — Number of parameters of the map (0, 1, or 2).

### Value and forward derivatives

- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward "forward()" — Evaluates the forward map \f$g(v)\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward_d1 "forward_d1()" — First derivative of the forward map, \f$g'(v)\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward_d2 "forward_d2()" — Second derivative of the forward map, \f$g''(v)\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward_d3 "forward_d3()" — Third derivative of the forward map, \f$g^{(3)}(v)\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward_d4 "forward_d4()" — Fourth derivative of the forward map, \f$g^{(4)}(v)\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward_d5 "forward_d5()" — Fifth derivative of the forward map, \f$g^{(5)}(v)\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward_d6 "forward_d6()" — Sixth derivative of the forward map, \f$g^{(6)}(v)\f$.

### Inverse value and inverse derivatives

- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse "inverse()" — Evaluates the inverse map \f$h(u)\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse_d1 "inverse_d1()" — First derivative of the inverse map, \f$h'(u)\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse_d2 "inverse_d2()" — Second derivative of the inverse map, \f$h''(u)\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse_d3 "inverse_d3()" — Third derivative of the inverse map, \f$h^{(3)}(u)\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse_d4 "inverse_d4()" — Fourth derivative of the inverse map, \f$h^{(4)}(u)\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse_d5 "inverse_d5()" — Fifth derivative of the inverse map, \f$h^{(5)}(u)\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse_d6 "inverse_d6()" — Sixth derivative of the inverse map, \f$h^{(6)}(u)\f$.

### Forward log-Jacobian and derivatives

- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward_log_jacobian "forward_log_jacobian()" — Forward log-Jacobian, \f$\log|g'(v)|\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward_log_jacobian_d1 "forward_log_jacobian_d1()" — First derivative of forward log-Jacobian, \f$\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}v}\log|g'(v)|\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward_log_jacobian_d2 "forward_log_jacobian_d2()" — Second derivative of forward log-Jacobian, \f$\frac{\mathrm{d}^2}{\mathrm{d}v^2}\log|g'(v)|\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward_log_jacobian_d3 "forward_log_jacobian_d3()" — Third derivative of forward log-Jacobian, \f$\frac{\mathrm{d}^3}{\mathrm{d}v^3}\log|g'(v)|\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward_log_jacobian_d4 "forward_log_jacobian_d4()" — Fourth derivative of forward log-Jacobian, \f$\frac{\mathrm{d}^4}{\mathrm{d}v^4}\log|g'(v)|\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward_log_jacobian_d5 "forward_log_jacobian_d5()" — Fifth derivative of forward log-Jacobian, \f$\frac{\mathrm{d}^5}{\mathrm{d}v^5}\log|g'(v)|\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::forward_log_jacobian_d6 "forward_log_jacobian_d6()" — Sixth derivative of forward log-Jacobian, \f$\frac{\mathrm{d}^6}{\mathrm{d}v^6}\log|g'(v)|\f$.

### Inverse log-Jacobian and derivatives

- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse_log_jacobian "inverse_log_jacobian()" — Inverse log-Jacobian, \f$\log|h'(u)|\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse_log_jacobian_d1 "inverse_log_jacobian_d1()" — First derivative of inverse log-Jacobian, \f$\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}u}\log|h'(u)|\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse_log_jacobian_d2 "inverse_log_jacobian_d2()" — Second derivative of inverse log-Jacobian, \f$\frac{\mathrm{d}^2}{\mathrm{d}u^2}\log|h'(u)|\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse_log_jacobian_d3 "inverse_log_jacobian_d3()" — Third derivative of inverse log-Jacobian, \f$\frac{\mathrm{d}^3}{\mathrm{d}u^3}\log|h'(u)|\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse_log_jacobian_d4 "inverse_log_jacobian_d4()" — Fourth derivative of inverse log-Jacobian, \f$\frac{\mathrm{d}^4}{\mathrm{d}u^4}\log|h'(u)|\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse_log_jacobian_d5 "inverse_log_jacobian_d5()" — Fifth derivative of inverse log-Jacobian, \f$\frac{\mathrm{d}^5}{\mathrm{d}u^5}\log|h'(u)|\f$.
- \ref laplace::bijector::scalar_bijector::inverse_log_jacobian_d6 "inverse_log_jacobian_d6()" — Sixth derivative of inverse log-Jacobian, \f$\frac{\mathrm{d}^6}{\mathrm{d}u^6}\log|h'(u)|\f$.

